IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-definitions`
IMPORT `coa16-part19-general`

-- coa16-part20-public-offers.l4: the Companies Act 2006, Part 20 (Private and public companies), Chapter 1
-- (Prohibition of public offers by private companies): ss 755 to 760 (lines 9813-9884 of ukpga-2006-46.txt).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".  Every `-- src:` line is generated by
-- srcrefs.py from that file (work/build.py), never retyped.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: see coa16-part19-general.l4 (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING and their comments).
-- Imports coa-definitions (the keel's `s 4(1)` private company, called directly) and coa16-part19-general (the s 738
-- kinds of instrument, for "securities" in s 755(5)).
--
-- NAMING.  A function named for a gate, an exclusion or a presumption answers JUST FALSE when its own limbs are not
-- met ("this provision does not apply"), never "the opposite substantive result": s 756(3) is named "the offer is
-- excluded ...", so JUST FALSE says "subsection (3) does not exclude it".

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Part 20 -- Chapter 1: Prohibition of public offers by private companies
-- =========================================================================================================

-- ---- s 756: Meaning of "offer to the public" (first, because s 755 uses it) -----------------------------------

-- src:9827 | 756 Meaning of “offer to the public”
-- src:9828 | (1) This section explains what is meant in this Chapter by an offer of securities to the public.
-- src:9829 | (2) An offer to the public includes an offer to any section of the public, however selected.
-- src:9830 | (3) An offer is not regarded as an offer to the public if it can properly be regarded, in all the circumstances, as—
-- src:9831 | (a) not being calculated to result, directly or indirectly, in securities of the company becoming available to persons other than those receiving the offer, or
-- src:9832 | (b) otherwise being a private concern of the person receiving it and the person making it.
-- src:9833 | (4) An offer is to be regarded (unless the contrary is proved) as being a private concern of the person receiving it and the person making it if—
-- src:9834 | (a) it is made to a person already connected with the company and, where it is made on terms allowing that person to renounce his rights, the rights may only be renounced in favour of another person already connected with the company; or
-- src:9835 | (b) it is an offer to subscribe for securities to be held under an employees' share scheme and, where it is made on terms allowing that person to renounce his rights, the rights may only be renounced in favour of—
-- src:9836 | (i) another person entitled to hold securities under the scheme, or
-- src:9837 | (ii) a person already connected with the company.
-- src:9838 | (5) For the purposes of this section “person already connected with the company” means—
-- src:9839 | (a) an existing member or employee of the company,
-- src:9840 | (b) a member of the family of a person who is or was a member or employee of the company,
-- src:9841 | (c) the widow or widower, or surviving civil partner, of a person who was a member or employee of the company,
-- src:9842 | (d) an existing debenture holder of the company, or
-- src:9843 | (e) a trustee (acting in his capacity as such) of a trust of which the principal beneficiary is a person within any of paragraphs (a) to (d).
-- src:9844 | (6) For the purposes of subsection (5)(b) the members of a person's family are the person's spouse or civil partner and children (including step-children) and their descendants.
@ref s 756 Meaning of "offer to the public" (src:9827-9844)
DECLARE `s 756(6) relationship to another person` HAS
    `s 756(6) the person is the other person's spouse or civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 756(6) the person is a child (including a step-child) of the other person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 756(6) the person is a descendant of such a child` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (6) "the members of a person's family are the person's spouse or civil partner and children (including
-- step-children) and their descendants": "are" closes the list, like "means" (fork F13).
@ref s 756(6) Meaning of "offer to the public": members of a person's family (src:9844)
GIVEN relationship IS A `s 756(6) relationship to another person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 756(6) the person is a member of the other person's family` MEANS
    IF       relationship's `s 756(6) the person is the other person's spouse or civil partner`
         OR  relationship's `s 756(6) the person is a child (including a step-child) of the other person`
         OR  relationship's `s 756(6) the person is a descendant of such a child`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the members of a person's family are the person's spouse or civil partner and children (including step-children) and their descendants"

DECLARE `s 756(5) facts about the person` HAS
    `s 756(5)(a) the person is an existing member of the company (s 112)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 756(5)(a) the person is an existing employee of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 756(5)(b) the person's relationship to a person who is or was a member or employee of the company` IS A `s 756(6) relationship to another person`
    `s 756(5)(c) the person is the widow or widower, or surviving civil partner, of a person who was a member or employee of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 756(5)(d) the person is an existing debenture holder of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 756(5)(e) the person is a trustee (acting in his capacity as such) of a trust of which the principal beneficiary is a person within any of paragraphs (a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (5) "“person already connected with the company” means (a) an existing member or employee of the company, (b) a
-- member of the family of a person who is or was a member or employee of the company, (c) the widow or widower, or
-- surviving civil partner, of a person who was a member or employee of the company, (d) an existing debenture holder
-- of the company, or (e) a trustee ... of a trust of which the principal beneficiary is a person within any of
-- paragraphs (a) to (d)."  Whether a person is a member is s 112 (an input, MAYBE BOOLEAN).
@ref s 756(5) Meaning of "offer to the public": person already connected with the company (src:9838-9843)
GIVEN person IS A `s 756(5) facts about the person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 756(5) the person is already connected with the company` MEANS
    IF       (person's `s 756(5)(a) the person is an existing member of the company (s 112)`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
         OR  person's `s 756(5)(a) the person is an existing employee of the company`
         OR  ((`s 756(6) the person is a member of the other person's family` (person's `s 756(5)(b) the person's relationship to a person who is or was a member or employee of the company`)) EQUALS (JUST TRUE))
         OR  person's `s 756(5)(c) the person is the widow or widower, or surviving civil partner, of a person who was a member or employee of the company`
         OR  person's `s 756(5)(d) the person is an existing debenture holder of the company`
         OR  person's `s 756(5)(e) the person is a trustee (acting in his capacity as such) of a trust of which the principal beneficiary is a person within any of paragraphs (a) to (d)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER person's `s 756(5)(a) the person is an existing member of the company (s 112)`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a member is s 112 and no other limb holds
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“person already connected with the company” means— (a) an existing member or employee of the company, (b) a member of the family of a person who is or was a member or employee of the company, (c) the widow or widower, or surviving civil partner, of a person who was a member or employee of the company, (d) an existing debenture holder of the company, or (e) a trustee"

DECLARE `s 756 offer` HAS
    `s 756(2) the offer is made to the public, or to a section of the public, however selected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 756(3)(a) it can properly be regarded, in all the circumstances, as not being calculated to result, directly or indirectly, in securities of the company becoming available to persons other than those receiving the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 756(3)(b) it can properly be regarded, in all the circumstances, as otherwise being a private concern of the person receiving it and the person making it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 756(4)(a) the offer is made to a person already connected with the company (s 756(5))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 756(4)(a) the offer is made on terms allowing that person to renounce his rights` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 756(4)(a) the rights may only be renounced in favour of another person already connected with the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 756(4)(b) the offer is an offer to subscribe for securities to be held under an employees' share scheme (s 1166)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 756(4)(b) the offer is made on terms allowing that person to renounce his rights` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 756(4)(b)(i) and (ii) the rights may only be renounced in favour of another person entitled to hold securities under the scheme or a person already connected with the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 756(4) the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (4)(a) "it is made to a person already connected with the company and, where it is made on terms allowing that
-- person to renounce his rights, the rights may only be renounced in favour of another person already connected
-- with the company".
@ref s 756(4) Meaning of "offer to the public": presumption, paragraph (a) (src:9833-9834)
GIVEN offer IS A `s 756 offer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 756(4)(a) the offer is made to a person already connected, on terms allowing renunciation only to such persons` MEANS
    CONSIDER offer's `s 756(4)(a) the offer is made to a person already connected with the company (s 756(5))`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF (NOT (offer's `s 756(4)(a) the offer is made on terms allowing that person to renounce his rights`)) OR offer's `s 756(4)(a) the rights may only be renounced in favour of another person already connected with the company`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) it is made to a person already connected with the company and, where it is made on terms allowing that person to renounce his rights, the rights may only be renounced in favour of another person already connected with the company"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) it is made to a person already connected with the company"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a member, an employee and so on is s 756(5) and s 112

-- (4)(b) "it is an offer to subscribe for securities to be held under an employees' share scheme and, where it is made
-- on terms allowing that person to renounce his rights, the rights may only be renounced in favour of (i) another
-- person entitled to hold securities under the scheme, or (ii) a person already connected with the company".
@ref s 756(4) Meaning of "offer to the public": presumption, paragraph (b) (src:9835-9837)
GIVEN offer IS A `s 756 offer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 756(4)(b) the offer is for securities to be held under an employees' share scheme, on terms allowing renunciation only to such persons` MEANS
    CONSIDER offer's `s 756(4)(b) the offer is an offer to subscribe for securities to be held under an employees' share scheme (s 1166)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF (NOT (offer's `s 756(4)(b) the offer is made on terms allowing that person to renounce his rights`)) OR offer's `s 756(4)(b)(i) and (ii) the rights may only be renounced in favour of another person entitled to hold securities under the scheme or a person already connected with the company`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) it is an offer to subscribe for securities to be held under an employees' share scheme and, where it is made on terms allowing that person to renounce his rights, the rights may only be renounced in favour of— (i) another person entitled to hold securities under the scheme, or (ii) a person already connected with the company"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) it is an offer to subscribe for securities to be held under an employees' share scheme"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the scheme is an employees' share scheme is s 1166

-- (4) "An offer is to be regarded (unless the contrary is proved) as being a private concern of the person receiving
-- it and the person making it if (a) ... or (b) ...".  The presumption applies when a limb is met and the contrary is
-- not proved (fork F14: "unless the contrary is proved" is a plain input, FALSE the ordinary case).
@ref s 756(4) Meaning of "offer to the public": the presumption (src:9833-9837)
GIVEN offer IS A `s 756 offer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 756(4) the presumption that the offer is a private concern applies` MEANS
    IF offer's `s 756(4) the contrary is proved`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An offer is to be regarded (unless the contrary is proved) as being a private concern"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 756(4)(a) the offer is made to a person already connected, on terms allowing renunciation only to such persons` offer
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN `s 756(4)(b) the offer is for securities to be held under an employees' share scheme, on terms allowing renunciation only to such persons` offer
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             CONSIDER `s 756(4)(b) the offer is for securities to be held under an employees' share scheme, on terms allowing renunciation only to such persons` offer
             WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
             OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): limb (a) depends on s 756(5) and s 112, which are not known

-- (3) "An offer is not regarded as an offer to the public if it can properly be regarded, in all the circumstances, as
-- (a) not being calculated to result, directly or indirectly, in securities of the company becoming available to
-- persons other than those receiving the offer, or (b) otherwise being a private concern of the person receiving it
-- and the person making it."  The presumption in (4) feeds limb (b).
@ref s 756(3) Meaning of "offer to the public": offers that are not offers to the public (src:9830-9832)
GIVEN offer IS A `s 756 offer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 756(3) the offer is excluded from being an offer to the public` MEANS
    IF       offer's `s 756(3)(a) it can properly be regarded, in all the circumstances, as not being calculated to result, directly or indirectly, in securities of the company becoming available to persons other than those receiving the offer`
         OR  offer's `s 756(3)(b) it can properly be regarded, in all the circumstances, as otherwise being a private concern of the person receiving it and the person making it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 756(4) the presumption that the offer is a private concern applies` offer
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE -- (4): the offer "is to be regarded ... as being a private concern", which is limb (b)
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An offer is not regarded as an offer to the public if it can properly be regarded, in all the circumstances, as"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the presumption in (4) depends on s 756(5), s 112 or s 1166

-- (2) "An offer to the public includes an offer to any section of the public, however selected."
@ref s 756(2) Meaning of "offer to the public": any section of the public (src:9829)
GIVEN offer IS A `s 756 offer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 756(2) the offer is an offer to the public by inclusion` MEANS
    IF offer's `s 756(2) the offer is made to the public, or to a section of the public, however selected`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "An offer to the public includes an offer to any section of the public"; what else is an offer to the public is not defined

-- (1) "This section explains what is meant in this Chapter by an offer of securities to the public": the whole of
-- s 756 as one answer.  An offer that subsection (3) excludes is not one; otherwise an offer to the public or to any
-- section of it is (fork F15: subsection (3) is applied before subsection (2)).
@ref s 756(1) Meaning of "offer to the public": the whole section (src:9828)
GIVEN offer IS A `s 756 offer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 756(1) the offer is an offer of securities to the public` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 756(3) the offer is excluded from being an offer to the public` offer
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An offer is not regarded as an offer to the public if it can properly be regarded, in all the circumstances, as"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether subsection (3) excludes the offer depends on s 756(5), s 112 or s 1166
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN `s 756(2) the offer is an offer to the public by inclusion` offer

-- ---- s 755: Prohibition of public offers by private company -----------------------------------------------------

-- src:9815 | 755 Prohibition of public offers by private company
-- src:9816 | (1) A private company limited by shares or limited by guarantee and having a share capital must not—
-- src:9817 | (a) offer to the public any securities of the company, or
-- src:9818 | (b) allot or agree to allot any securities of the company with a view to their being offered to the public.
-- src:9819 | (2) Unless the contrary is proved, an allotment or agreement to allot securities is presumed to be made with a view to their being offered to the public if an offer of the securities (or any of them) to the public is made—
-- src:9820 | (a) within six months after the allotment or agreement to allot, or
-- src:9821 | (b) before the receipt by the company of the whole of the consideration to be received by it in respect of the securities.
-- src:9822 | (3) A company does not contravene this section if—
-- src:9823 | (a) it acts in good faith in pursuance of arrangements under which it is to re-register as a public company before the securities are allotted, or
-- src:9824 | (b) as part of the terms of the offer it undertakes to re-register as a public company within a specified period, and that undertaking is complied with.
-- src:9825 | (4) The specified period for the purposes of subsection (3)(b) must be a period ending not later than six months after the day on which the offer is made (or, in the case of an offer made on different days, first made).
-- src:9826 | (5) In this Chapter “securities” means shares or debentures.
@ref s 755 Prohibition of public offers by private company (src:9815-9826)
DECLARE `s 755 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 755 offer securities of the company to the public`
    `s 755 allot or agree to allot securities of the company with a view to their being offered to the public`

-- (5) "In this Chapter “securities” means shares or debentures."  A debenture is s 738 (the question arises in this
-- Act, so the Companies Acts limb is JUST TRUE).
@ref s 755(5) Prohibition of public offers by private company: securities (src:9826)
GIVEN instrument IS A `s 738 kind of instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 755(5) the instrument is a security for this Chapter` MEANS
    CONSIDER instrument
    WHEN `s 738 a share in a company` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` instrument FALSE (JUST TRUE)

-- (1) "A private company limited by shares or limited by guarantee and having a share capital must not ...".  The
-- company must be a private company (the keel's s 4(1)); the share capital qualifies the guarantee limb (fork F12).
@ref s 755(1) Prohibition of public offers by private company: the company the prohibition binds (src:9816)
GIVEN company IS A `Company profile`
      `the requirements as to registration or re-registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date (s 4(2)(b))` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 755(1) the company is within the prohibition` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 4(1) the company is a private company` company `the requirements as to registration or re-registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date (s 4(2)(b))`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF       company's `liability of the members` EQUALS `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held`
             OR (    company's `liability of the members` EQUALS `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up`
                 AND company's `a share capital`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private company limited by shares or limited by guarantee and having a share capital"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private company"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): follows s 4

-- (1)(a) "offer to the public any securities of the company": the offer is s 756, the securities s 755(5).
@ref s 755(1) Prohibition of public offers by private company: paragraph (a) (src:9817)
GIVEN `the company has made an offer of the securities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is a security for this Chapter (s 755(5))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offer is an offer of securities to the public (s 756(1))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 755(1)(a) the company offers securities of the company to the public` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company has made an offer of the securities`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "offer to the public any securities of the company"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the instrument is a security for this Chapter (s 755(5))`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `the offer is an offer of securities to the public (s 756(1))`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any securities of the company": "securities" means shares or debentures
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the instrument is a debenture is s 738

-- (2) "Unless the contrary is proved, an allotment or agreement to allot securities is presumed to be made with a
-- view to their being offered to the public if an offer of the securities (or any of them) to the public is made (a)
-- within six months after the allotment or agreement to allot, or (b) before the receipt by the company of the whole
-- of the consideration to be received by it in respect of the securities."  Six months is `add months`, the last
-- day counted in time; "before the receipt" is strictly before (fork F16).
@ref s 755(2) Prohibition of public offers by private company: the presumption, paragraph (a) (src:9820)
GIVEN `the date of the allotment or agreement to allot` IS A DATE
      `the date the offer is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 755(2)(a) the offer is made within six months after the allotment or agreement to allot` MEANS
        `the date the offer is made` AT LEAST `the date of the allotment or agreement to allot`
    AND `the date the offer is made` AT MOST (`add months` `the date of the allotment or agreement to allot` 6)

@ref s 755(2) Prohibition of public offers by private company: the presumption, paragraph (b) (src:9821)
GIVEN `the date the offer is made` IS A DATE
      `the date the company received the whole of the consideration, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 755(2)(b) the offer is made before the company receives the whole of the consideration` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the company received the whole of the consideration, if it has`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST received THEN `the date the offer is made` LESS THAN received

@ref s 755(2) Prohibition of public offers by private company: the presumption (src:9819-9821)
GIVEN `an offer of the securities (or any of them) to the public is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the allotment or agreement to allot` IS A DATE
      `the date the offer is made` IS A DATE
      `the date the company received the whole of the consideration, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 755(2) the presumption that the allotment was made with a view to the securities being offered to the public applies` MEANS
    IF `the contrary is proved`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the contrary is proved, an allotment or agreement to allot securities is presumed to be made with a view to their being offered to the public"
    ELSE IF       `an offer of the securities (or any of them) to the public is made`
              AND (    `s 755(2)(a) the offer is made within six months after the allotment or agreement to allot` `the date of the allotment or agreement to allot` `the date the offer is made`
                   OR `s 755(2)(b) the offer is made before the company receives the whole of the consideration` `the date the offer is made` `the date the company received the whole of the consideration, if it has`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if an offer of the securities (or any of them) to the public is made (a) within six months after the allotment or agreement to allot, or (b) before the receipt by the company of the whole of the consideration to be received by it in respect of the securities"

-- (1)(b) "allot or agree to allot any securities of the company with a view to their being offered to the public":
-- the view is a fact, or presumed under (2).
@ref s 755(1) Prohibition of public offers by private company: paragraph (b) (src:9818)
GIVEN `the company has allotted or agreed to allot the securities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is a security for this Chapter (s 755(5))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the allotment was in fact made with a view to the securities being offered to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the presumption in subsection (2) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 755(1)(b) the company allots or agrees to allot securities with a view to their being offered to the public` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company has allotted or agreed to allot the securities`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "allot or agree to allot any securities of the company with a view to their being offered to the public"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the instrument is a security for this Chapter (s 755(5))`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             IF `the allotment was in fact made with a view to the securities being offered to the public` OR ((`the presumption in subsection (2) applies`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE))
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with a view to their being offered to the public"
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any securities of the company"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the instrument is a debenture is s 738

-- (4) "The specified period for the purposes of subsection (3)(b) must be a period ending not later than six months
-- after the day on which the offer is made (or, in the case of an offer made on different days, first made)."
@ref s 755(4) Prohibition of public offers by private company: the specified period (src:9825)
GIVEN `the day on which the offer is made (or, if made on different days, first made)` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the specified period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 755(4) the specified period ends in time` MEANS
    IF `the last day of the specified period` AT MOST (`add months` `the day on which the offer is made (or, if made on different days, first made)` 6)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be a period ending not later than six months after the day on which the offer is made"

-- (3) "A company does not contravene this section if (a) it acts in good faith in pursuance of arrangements under
-- which it is to re-register as a public company before the securities are allotted, or (b) as part of the terms of
-- the offer it undertakes to re-register as a public company within a specified period, and that undertaking is
-- complied with."  When neither limb holds the exception is not made out (fork F17).
@ref s 755(3) Prohibition of public offers by private company: the exceptions (src:9822-9824)
GIVEN `the company acts in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company acts in pursuance of arrangements under which it is to re-register as a public company before the securities are allotted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `as part of the terms of the offer the company undertakes to re-register as a public company within a specified period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that undertaking is complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the offer is made (or, if made on different days, first made)` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the specified period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 755(3) the company is excepted from the prohibition` MEANS
    IF       (`the company acts in good faith` AND `the company acts in pursuance of arrangements under which it is to re-register as a public company before the securities are allotted`)
         OR  (    `as part of the terms of the offer the company undertakes to re-register as a public company within a specified period`
              AND `that undertaking is complied with`
              AND ((`s 755(4) the specified period ends in time` `the day on which the offer is made (or, if made on different days, first made)` `the last day of the specified period`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company does not contravene this section if (a) it acts in good faith in pursuance of arrangements under which it is to re-register as a public company before the securities are allotted, or (b) as part of the terms of the offer it undertakes to re-register as a public company within a specified period, and that undertaking is complied with" (this exception is not made out)

-- The prohibition as a whole: within it, one of the two acts, and not excepted.  A company that does not contravene
-- because of subsection (3) answers JUST FALSE ("does not contravene").
@ref s 755(1) Prohibition of public offers by private company: the contravention (src:9816-9824)
GIVEN `the company is within the prohibition (s 755(1))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company offers securities to the public (s 755(1)(a))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company allots or agrees to allot with a view to a public offer (s 755(1)(b))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company is excepted (s 755(3))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 755(1) the company contravenes the prohibition, subject to subsection (3)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the company is within the prohibition (s 755(1))`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF ((`the company offers securities to the public (s 755(1)(a))`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)) OR ((`the company allots or agrees to allot with a view to a public offer (s 755(1)(b))`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE))
        THEN
            CONSIDER `the company is excepted (s 755(3))`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company does not contravene this section if"
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the exception applies is not known
        ELSE IF ((`the company offers securities to the public (s 755(1)(a))`) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)) AND ((`the company allots or agrees to allot with a view to a public offer (s 755(1)(b))`) EQUALS (JUST FALSE))
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not— (a) offer to the public any securities of the company, or (b) allot or agree to allot any securities of the company with a view to their being offered to the public"
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): neither act is shown to be done
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private company limited by shares or limited by guarantee and having a share capital"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private company limited by shares or limited by guarantee and having a share capital"

-- The prohibition as a regulative rule: for a company within it, a SHANT for each act.
@ref s 755(1) Prohibition of public offers by private company: the prohibition (src:9816-9818)
GIVEN `the company is within the prohibition (s 755(1))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 755 act`
`s 755(1) the company must not offer securities to the public or allot them with a view to a public offer` MEANS
    IF (`the company is within the prohibition (s 755(1))`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN (PARTY Company
          SHANT `s 755 offer securities of the company to the public`
          HENCE FULFILLED
          LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 755(1)(a): a private company offered securities of the company to the public")
         RAND
         (PARTY Company
          SHANT `s 755 allot or agree to allot securities of the company with a view to their being offered to the public`
          HENCE FULFILLED
          LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 755(1)(b): a private company allotted or agreed to allot securities with a view to their being offered to the public")
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- ---- s 757: Enforcement of prohibition: order restraining proposed contravention ---------------------------------

-- src:9845 | 757 Enforcement of prohibition: order restraining proposed contravention
-- src:9846 | (1) If it appears to the court—
-- src:9847 | (a) on an application under this section, or
-- src:9848 | (b) in proceedings under Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice),
-- src:9849 | that a company is proposing to act in contravention of section 755 (prohibition of public offers by private companies), the court shall make an order under this section.
-- src:9850 | (2) An order under this section is an order restraining the company from contravening that section.
-- src:9851 | (3) An application for an order under this section may be made by—
-- src:9852 | (a) a member or creditor of the company, or
-- src:9853 | (b) the Secretary of State.
@ref s 757 Enforcement of prohibition: order restraining proposed contravention (src:9845-9853)
DECLARE `s 757 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 757 make an order restraining the company from contravening section 755`

-- (1) "If it appears to the court (a) on an application under this section, or (b) in proceedings under Part 30 ...
-- that a company is proposing to act in contravention of section 755, the court shall make an order under this
-- section."  Part 30 is another part's (coa22): a plain fact that such proceedings are on foot.
@ref s 757(1) Enforcement of prohibition: the court's duty (src:9846-9849)
GIVEN `it appears to the court that a company is proposing to act in contravention of section 755` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is hearing an application under section 757` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is hearing proceedings under Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 757(1) the court shall make an order restraining the company` MEANS
    IF       `it appears to the court that a company is proposing to act in contravention of section 755`
         AND (`the court is hearing an application under section 757` OR `the court is hearing proceedings under Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If it appears to the court— (a) on an application under this section, or (b) in proceedings under Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice), that a company is proposing to act in contravention of section 755 (prohibition of public offers by private companies), the court shall make an order under this section"

@ref s 757(1) Enforcement of prohibition: the court's duty as a regulative rule (src:9846-9849)
GIVEN `the court shall make an order (s 757(1))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 757 act`
`s 757(1) the court must make the order` MEANS
    IF (`the court shall make an order (s 757(1))`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN PARTY Court
         MUST `s 757 make an order restraining the company from contravening section 755`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (2) "An order under this section is an order restraining the company from contravening that section."  "is" is read
-- as a definition and closed (fork F18).
@ref s 757(2) Enforcement of prohibition: the order (src:9850)
GIVEN `the order restrains the company from contravening section 755` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 757(2) the order is an order under this section` MEANS
    IF `the order restrains the company from contravening section 755`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An order under this section is an order restraining the company from contravening that section"

-- (3) "An application for an order under this section may be made by (a) a member or creditor of the company, or (b)
-- the Secretary of State."  The list is not closed with "only".
@ref s 757(3) Enforcement of prohibition: who may apply (src:9851-9853)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company (s 112)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a creditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 757(3) the person may apply for an order under this section` MEANS
    IF `the person is a creditor of the company` OR `the person is the Secretary of State` OR ((`the person is a member of the company (s 112)`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be made by (a) a member or creditor of the company, or (b) the Secretary of State"

-- ---- s 758: Enforcement of prohibition: orders available to the court after contravention ---------------------------

-- src:9854 | 758 Enforcement of prohibition: orders available to the court after contravention
-- src:9855 | (1) This section applies if it appears to the court—
-- src:9856 | (a) on an application under this section, or
-- src:9857 | (b) in proceedings under Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice),
-- src:9858 | that a company has acted in contravention of section 755 (prohibition of public offers by private companies).
-- src:9859 | (2) The court must make an order requiring the company to re-register as a public company unless it appears to the court—
-- src:9860 | (a) that the company does not meet the requirements for re-registration as a public company, and
-- src:9861 | (b) that it is impractical or undesirable to require it to take steps to do so.
-- src:9862 | (3) If it does not make an order for re-registration, the court may make either or both of the following—
-- src:9863 | (a) a remedial order (see section 759), or
-- src:9864 | (b) an order for the compulsory winding up of the company.
-- src:9865 | (4) An application under this section may be made by—
-- src:9866 | (a) a member of the company who—
-- src:9867 | (i) was a member at the time the offer was made (or, if the offer was made over a period, at any time during that period), or
-- src:9868 | (ii) became a member as a result of the offer,
-- src:9869 | (b) a creditor of the company who was a creditor at the time the offer was made (or, if the offer was made over a period, at any time during that period), or
-- src:9870 | (c) the Secretary of State.
@ref s 758 Enforcement of prohibition: orders available to the court after contravention (src:9854-9870)
DECLARE `s 758 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 758 make an order requiring the company to re-register as a public company`

-- (1) "This section applies if it appears to the court (a) on an application under this section, or (b) in
-- proceedings under Part 30 ... that a company has acted in contravention of section 755."
@ref s 758(1) Enforcement of prohibition after contravention: when the section applies (src:9855-9858)
GIVEN `it appears to the court that a company has acted in contravention of section 755` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is hearing an application under section 758` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is hearing proceedings under Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 758(1) the section applies` MEANS
    IF       `it appears to the court that a company has acted in contravention of section 755`
         AND (`the court is hearing an application under section 758` OR `the court is hearing proceedings under Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies if it appears to the court— (a) on an application under this section, or (b) in proceedings under Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice), that a company has acted in contravention of section 755"

-- (2) "The court must make an order requiring the company to re-register as a public company unless it appears to the
-- court (a) that the company does not meet the requirements for re-registration as a public company, and (b) that it
-- is impractical or undesirable to require it to take steps to do so."  The exception needs both limbs.
@ref s 758(2) Enforcement of prohibition after contravention: the order to re-register (src:9859-9861)
GIVEN `it appears to the court that a company has acted in contravention of section 755` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is hearing an application under section 758` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is hearing proceedings under Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the court that the company does not meet the requirements for re-registration as a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the court that it is impractical or undesirable to require the company to take steps to re-register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 758(2) the court must make an order requiring the company to re-register as a public company` MEANS
    IF ((`s 758(1) the section applies` `it appears to the court that a company has acted in contravention of section 755` `the court is hearing an application under section 758` `the court is hearing proceedings under Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice)`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE))
    THEN
        IF       `it appears to the court that the company does not meet the requirements for re-registration as a public company`
             AND `it appears to the court that it is impractical or undesirable to require the company to take steps to re-register`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it appears to the court (a) that the company does not meet the requirements for re-registration as a public company, and (b) that it is impractical or undesirable to require it to take steps to do so"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies if it appears to the court"

@ref s 758(2) Enforcement of prohibition after contravention: the duty as a regulative rule (src:9859-9861)
GIVEN `the court must make an order to re-register (s 758(2))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 758 act`
`s 758(2) the court must order the company to re-register` MEANS
    IF (`the court must make an order to re-register (s 758(2))`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN PARTY Court
         MUST `s 758 make an order requiring the company to re-register as a public company`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (3) "If it does not make an order for re-registration, the court may make either or both of the following (a) a
-- remedial order (see section 759), or (b) an order for the compulsory winding up of the company."
@ref s 758(3) Enforcement of prohibition after contravention: remedial order or winding up (src:9862-9864)
GIVEN `it appears to the court that a company has acted in contravention of section 755` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is hearing an application under section 758` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is hearing proceedings under Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has not made an order for re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 758(3)(a) the court may make a remedial order` MEANS
    IF       ((`s 758(1) the section applies` `it appears to the court that a company has acted in contravention of section 755` `the court is hearing an application under section 758` `the court is hearing proceedings under Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice)`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE))
         AND `the court has not made an order for re-registration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If it does not make an order for re-registration, the court may make either or both of the following"

@ref s 758(3) Enforcement of prohibition after contravention: compulsory winding up (src:9862-9864)
GIVEN `it appears to the court that a company has acted in contravention of section 755` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is hearing an application under section 758` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is hearing proceedings under Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has not made an order for re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 758(3)(b) the court may make an order for the compulsory winding up of the company` MEANS
    IF       ((`s 758(1) the section applies` `it appears to the court that a company has acted in contravention of section 755` `the court is hearing an application under section 758` `the court is hearing proceedings under Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice)`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE))
         AND `the court has not made an order for re-registration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If it does not make an order for re-registration, the court may make either or both of the following"

-- (4) "An application under this section may be made by (a) a member of the company who (i) was a member at the time the
-- offer was made (or, if the offer was made over a period, at any time during that period), or (ii) became a member as
-- a result of the offer, (b) a creditor of the company who was a creditor at the time the offer was made (or ...
-- during that period), or (c) the Secretary of State."
@ref s 758(4) Enforcement of prohibition after contravention: who may apply (src:9865-9870)
GIVEN `the person was a member of the company at the time the offer was made (or, if the offer was made over a period, at any time during that period)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person became a member of the company as a result of the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was a creditor of the company at the time the offer was made (or, if the offer was made over a period, at any time during that period)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 758(4) the person may apply for an order under this section` MEANS
    IF       `the person was a member of the company at the time the offer was made (or, if the offer was made over a period, at any time during that period)`
         OR  `the person became a member of the company as a result of the offer`
         OR  `the person was a creditor of the company at the time the offer was made (or, if the offer was made over a period, at any time during that period)`
         OR  `the person is the Secretary of State`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "An application under this section may be made by"

-- ---- s 759: Enforcement of prohibition: remedial order --------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9871 | 759 Enforcement of prohibition: remedial order
-- src:9872 | (1) A “remedial order” is an order for the purpose of putting a person affected by anything done in contravention of section 755 (prohibition of public offers by private company) in the position he would have been in if it had not been done.
-- src:9873 | (2) The following provisions are without prejudice to the generality of the power to make such an order.
-- src:9874 | (3) Where a private company has—
-- src:9875 | (a) allotted securities pursuant to an offer to the public, or
-- src:9876 | (b) allotted or agreed to allot securities with a view to their being offered to the public,
-- src:9877 | a remedial order may require any person knowingly concerned in the contravention of section 755 to offer to purchase any of those securities at such price and on such other terms as the court thinks fit.
-- src:9878 | (4) A remedial order may be made—
-- src:9879 | (a) against any person knowingly concerned in the contravention, whether or not an officer of the company;
-- src:9880 | (b) notwithstanding anything in the company's constitution (which includes, for this purpose, the terms on which any securities of the company are allotted or held);
-- src:9881 | (c) whether or not the holder of the securities subject to the order is the person to whom the company allotted or agreed to allot them.
-- src:9882 | (5) Where a remedial order is made against the company itself, the court may provide for the reduction of the company's capital accordingly.
@ref s 759 Enforcement of prohibition: remedial order (src:9871-9882)
GIVEN `the order is for the purpose of putting a person affected by anything done in contravention of section 755 in the position he would have been in if it had not been done` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 759(1) the order is a remedial order` MEANS
    IF `the order is for the purpose of putting a person affected by anything done in contravention of section 755 in the position he would have been in if it had not been done`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “remedial order” is an order for the purpose of putting a person affected by anything done in contravention of section 755 in the position he would have been in if it had not been done"

-- (2) "The following provisions are without prejudice to the generality of the power to make such an order."  A
-- remedial order may take a form that subsections (3) to (5) do not list: the answer does not read that fact.
@ref s 759(2) Enforcement of prohibition: the generality of the power (src:9873)
GIVEN `the order is a remedial order (s 759(1))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the form of order is one that subsections (3) to (5) list` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 759(2) the court may make a remedial order of this form` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the order is a remedial order (s 759(1))`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE -- listed or not: "without prejudice to the generality of the power to make such an order"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the power to make such an order"

-- (3) "Where a private company has (a) allotted securities pursuant to an offer to the public, or (b) allotted or agreed
-- to allot securities with a view to their being offered to the public, a remedial order may require any person
-- knowingly concerned in the contravention of section 755 to offer to purchase any of those securities at such price
-- and on such other terms as the court thinks fit."
-- The gate "Where a private company has (a) ... or (b) ..." is of the "where" kind: listed in the name-test sweep (fork F37), not flipped,
-- so JUST FALSE when it fails; a person who is not knowingly concerned is outside the grant's own limit: NOTHING.
@ref s 759(3) Enforcement of prohibition: an order to offer to purchase (src:9874-9877)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has allotted securities pursuant to an offer to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has allotted or agreed to allot securities with a view to their being offered to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is knowingly concerned in the contravention of section 755` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 759(3) a remedial order may require the person to offer to purchase the securities` MEANS
    IF NOT (       `the company is a private company`
               AND (`the company has allotted securities pursuant to an offer to the public` OR `the company has allotted or agreed to allot securities with a view to their being offered to the public`))
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a private company has (a) allotted securities pursuant to an offer to the public, or (b) allotted or agreed to allot securities with a view to their being offered to the public"
    ELSE IF `the person is knowingly concerned in the contravention of section 755`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person knowingly concerned in the contravention of section 755"

-- (4)(a) "A remedial order may be made against any person knowingly concerned in the contravention, whether or not an
-- officer of the company."
@ref s 759(4) Enforcement of prohibition: against whom (src:9879)
GIVEN `the person is knowingly concerned in the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 759(4)(a) a remedial order may be made against the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is knowingly concerned in the contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- whether or not an officer: the answer does not read that fact
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against any person knowingly concerned in the contravention"

-- (4)(b) "notwithstanding anything in the company's constitution (which includes, for this purpose, the terms on which
-- any securities of the company are allotted or held)".
@ref s 759(4) Enforcement of prohibition: despite the constitution (src:9880)
GIVEN `the company's constitution (including the terms on which the securities are allotted or held) provides to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 759(4)(b) a remedial order may be made despite the company's constitution` MEANS
    JUST TRUE -- the answer does not read the constitution: "notwithstanding anything in the company's constitution"

-- (4)(c) "whether or not the holder of the securities subject to the order is the person to whom the company allotted
-- or agreed to allot them."
@ref s 759(4) Enforcement of prohibition: whoever holds the securities (src:9881)
GIVEN `the holder of the securities subject to the order is the person to whom the company allotted or agreed to allot them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 759(4)(c) a remedial order may be made whoever now holds the securities` MEANS
    JUST TRUE -- the answer does not read who holds them: "whether or not the holder of the securities subject to the order is the person to whom the company allotted or agreed to allot them"

-- (5) "Where a remedial order is made against the company itself, the court may provide for the reduction of the
-- company's capital accordingly."
-- The gate is of the "where" kind: listed in the name-test sweep (fork F38), not flipped, so JUST FALSE when it fails.
@ref s 759(5) Enforcement of prohibition: reduction of capital (src:9882)
GIVEN `a remedial order is made against the company itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 759(5) the court may provide for the reduction of the company's capital` MEANS
    IF `a remedial order is made against the company itself`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a remedial order is made against the company itself"

-- ---- s 760: Validity of allotment etc not affected -------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9883 | 760 Validity of allotment etc not affected
-- src:9884 | Nothing in this Chapter affects the validity of any allotment or sale of securities or of any agreement to allot or sell securities.
@ref s 760 Validity of allotment etc not affected (src:9883-9884)
DECLARE `s 760 transaction` IS ONE OF
    `s 760 an allotment of securities`
    `s 760 a sale of securities`
    `s 760 an agreement to allot securities`
    `s 760 an agreement to sell securities`
    `s 760 any other transaction`

@ref s 760 Validity of allotment etc not affected (src:9884)
GIVEN transaction IS A `s 760 transaction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 760 this Chapter affects the validity of the transaction` MEANS
    CONSIDER transaction
    WHEN `s 760 any other transaction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any allotment or sale of securities or of any agreement to allot or sell securities"
